Frostbrand is a *GREAT* weapon, even unenchanted. It chops stuff up
magnificently, and having it given to you by your god means that you can
train longsword up to basic proficiency to skip out on the to-hit and
damage penalties.

>I've got TC and teleportitis, but Medusa is no-teleport.  I could try
>to get a wish out of a lamp and blow it on a cockatrice corpse, but
>that's about the only idea I have right now.  What else can I do?

You could just wander around a bit until a real cockatrice comes up,
instead of wasting a wish on one. If you have a wand or spellbook of create
monster, you can hasten this process. The wandering around will also get
you up to level 14 so you can do the Quest (which is pretty easy for
Wizards). The Eye would be a huge boon.

Since you have 2 lamps, I'd bless and rub one and wish for some +2 SDSM.
Will mean a *huge* upgrade in your AC, and will solve the issue of getting
reflection. Burning the second lamp is up to you. I wouldn't, as I *really*
like having it as a permenant light source for Gehennom. The Castle wand of
wishing is only 2-3 levels away.

Have you dug out the pre-medusa levels and looked for Ludios? If it exists
in your game, then you have a bountiful supply of money to buy a bunch of
protection with and improve your AC even further. Plus there's a
better-than-decent chance of getting some useable items. Soldiers are good
for wands/scrolls and other useful things like pre-enchanted leather
gloves/boots.


